Value Required LOCAL_INTERFACE (\S+)
Value CHASSIS_ID (\S+)
Value NEIGHBOR_PORT_ID (.*)
Value NEIGHBOR_NAME (.*)
Value NEIGHBOR_DESCRIPTION (.*)
Value MGMT_ADDRESS (.*)
Value CAPABILITIES (.*)

# Built from, and confirmed live (2026-08-21) against, a real ArubaOS-
# Switch (ProVision) 3810M running an actual crawl. The implicit-EOF-Record
# assumption (no explicit EOF state defined; see tfsm_test.go) is confirmed
# working -- the last neighbor block in a real capture has no trailing
# separator before the stripped prompt, and it still gets recorded.
#
# MGMT_ADDRESS is `(.*)`, not `(\S+)`: a live capture had a neighbor whose
# Remote Management Address Type was "all802" rather than "ipv4", with the
# address given as six space-separated hex byte pairs ("02 00 00 00 51 20")
# instead of a single dotted-quad token. `\S+` could not match past the
# first byte and fell through to the catch-all Error rule.
#
# Record boundary is the next "Local Port :" line rather than the trailing
# dash separator, because the LAST block in a real capture has no trailing
# separator before the stripped prompt — same idiom juniper_junos's detail
# template already uses.
#
# Confirmed live (2026-08-26) against a real ArubaOS-Switch stack: several
# neighbors' MED/PoE detail carries fields this template never saw when it
# was built -- "Media Policy Vlan id   :150", "Power Requested        :25.0
# W" -- and both fell into the trailing `^.* -> Error` catch-all, aborting
# the ENTIRE parse for that device. Since this platform is BestEffort (see
# plan.go) specifically because its real-world output keeps proving more
# varied than any one capture anticipated, the catch-all was changed from
# erroring out to matching and silently dropping the line, the same fix
# aruba_cx's template needed for the same reason: an unrecognized line
# should cost at most the field it was on, never the rest of the device's
# neighbors.
Start
  ^\s*Local\s+Port\s*:\s*\S+\s*$$ -> Continue.Record
  ^\s*Local\s+Port\s*:\s*${LOCAL_INTERFACE}\s*$$
  ^\s*ChassisType\s*:
  ^\s*ChassisId\s*:\s*${CHASSIS_ID}\s*$$
  ^\s*PortType\s*:
  ^\s*PortId\s*:\s*${NEIGHBOR_PORT_ID}\s*$$
  ^\s*SysName\s*:\s*${NEIGHBOR_NAME}\s*$$
  ^\s*System\s+Descr\s*:\s*${NEIGHBOR_DESCRIPTION}\s*$$
  ^\s*PortDescr\s*:
  ^\s*Pvid\s*:
  ^\s*System\s+Capabilities\s+Supported\s*:
  ^\s*System\s+Capabilities\s+Enabled\s*:\s*${CAPABILITIES}\s*$$
  ^\s*Remote\s+Management\s+Address\s*$$
  ^\s*Type\s*:
  ^\s*Address\s*:\s*${MGMT_ADDRESS}\s*$$
  ^\s*MED\s+Information\s+Detail\s*$$
  ^\s*EndpointClass
  ^\s*Poe\s+Plus\s+Information\s+Detail\s*$$
  ^\s*Poe\s+Device\s+Type\s*:
  ^\s*Power\s+Source\s*:
  ^\s*Power\s+Priority\s*:
  ^\s*PD\s+Requested\s+Power\s+Value\s*:
  ^\s*PSE\s+Allocated\s+Power\s+Value\s*:
  ^-+\s*$$
  ^\s*LLDP\s+Remote\s+Device\s+Information\s+Detail\s*$$
  ^\s*$$
  ^.*
